From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:26:04 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 66/72] deepseek: read the ported image, Engram and memo
 settings through the shared table

The settings G's line added (TF_DSV41_GRAMMAR, ENGRAM_VALIDATE, ENGRAM_DIR,
PF_SCRATCH_ALIAS, TOKENIZER_MESSAGE_MEMO, VISION_MAX_IMAGES, VISION_CACHE_MB,
KV_MIRROR) get rows in platform/environment.zig, so startup refuses malformed
text by name and lean_check finds no direct reads. environment.readText gives
a presence row's text (BIAS_VL's and ENGRAM_DIR's directories). Each reader
keeps its own error and its default for unset or blank text.

The retained-model registry moves to model_retain.zig, firstSplit to steps.zig
and two test blocks merge, so no file passes 600 lines.
